sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphological realism / specimen match: 63/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Judged on the PNG gallery and the GIF, the tunnel panel is a convincing set of concentric rings with tangential line elements, the oblique roll pulls back to a clearly chiral logarithmic spiral, and the square lattice gives a radial-plus-circular cobweb that resembles Bressloff's Fig. 31; the four families are visually distinct. Deductions: the spiral is not continuous - the full-field convention leaves a seam on the left horizontal meridian with 9.9x row-to-row contrast that I computed to span 0.8 wavelengths at 10 deg and 0.23 at 40 deg, and it is visible in both the PNG and GIF frame 8, whereas Klüver's spirals are continuous (-10); the contoured honeycomb panel reads as a hexagonal lattice of blobs rather than a honeycomb (the non- contoured GIF frame does show cells) (-4); the fifth panel, the only one the model actually selects, is a rhombic blob field that corresponds to no reported form constant, so the model's own choice does not look like a Klüver class (-6); at 11 rings per 40 deg the pullbacks are coarser than the 30-36 stripes the paper quotes from subjects (-5); there is no side-by-side with Klüver's or Bressloff Fig. 1 / Ermentrout-Cowan drawings in the figure, so the match is left to the viewer (-5); the honest SELECTED/IMPOSED badging is credited and prevents a larger deduction for imposing three of the four forms. Evidence: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): Row 2: rings/tunnel and cobweb convincing; spiral chiral but with visible left-meridian seam; honeycomb renders as blob lattice; rhombic (SELECTED) resembles no Klüver class — bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at d6f3c94, image/png, 1634872 B, 2620×2419 px, artifact_sha256 799d93639f28fa0f81279848de4b8d23b26644a1c8856fdc44c0028d4fc6ba5e (sha256 799d93639f28fa0f81279848de4b8d23b26644a1c8856fdc44c0028d4fc6ba5e), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif (generated output, not in repo): Frame 8 (spiral) shows the seam across the left half of the disc; frame 22 (honeycomb, non-contoured) shows clear hexagonal cells — docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at d6f3c94, image/gif, 2349709 B, 640×350 px, 36 frames, artifact_sha256 db057a32f49451a8c5ada9698336085308e9d3664d17769f51fa1cf4dda4dae8 (sha256 db057a32f49451a8c5ada9698336085308e9d3664d17769f51fa1cf4dda4dae8), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1102–L1118: Full-field theta_map = arctan2(v, u) default; bilateral-mirror reflects the same mode so spirals become chevrons (mirror_symmetry 1.000 for all five presets) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1102-L1118>; bressloff_v1_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): kluver_form_constant rows: spiral seam_contrast=9.91, rendered_cycles=11 for all five panels, three panels IMPOSED-UNSTABLE — bressloff_v1_metrics.csv: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at d6f3c94, text/csv, 10879 B, artifact_sha256 0aabf307f1e286177538d3bf61be79bc46f056afbf2303ee3c7e55229f6b7c35 (sha256 0aabf307f1e286177538d3bf61be79bc46f056afbf2303ee3c7e55229f6b7c35), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.63"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Morphological realism / specimen match' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

